      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Repeated unexpected faults can busy-loop the resident process",
      "description": "The exception handler always reports work after escalating. But escalation may write nothing when the node is already blocked or the project escalation is already open (`src/amoeba/runner/faults.py:171-190`). The host waits for its idle interval only when no tenant reports work (`src/amoeba/process/host.py:251-254`), so a recurring planner or stage exception can make the Runner retry continuously and consume CPU. Report work only when escalation actually changed state, or otherwise allow the host to idle.",
